  ### @brief Initial SPI Mode
  ### @details This option selects the SPI bus mode after a reset. The original
  ### SPI bus used only 1 wire for information transfer; this is known as 'normal mode'.
  ### Later, to improve transfer speeds, additional lines were added and
  ### thus was added 'Dual mode' and 'Quad mode'. The numbers following the mode
  ### names below show how the information is transferred, e.g. the number of
  ### lines used. The first number is for the command, the 2nd for the address
  ### and the 3rd is for the data.
  ### @li 0 Use power up default
  ### @li 1 Normal read (up to 33MHz)
  ### @li 2 Dual IO (1-1-2)
  ### @li 3 Quad IO (1-1-4)
  ### @li 4 Dual IO (1-2-2)
  ### @li 5 Quad IO (1-4-4)
  ### @li 6 Normal Read (up to 66MHz)
  ### @li 7 Fast Read commands
  gEfiAmdAgesaModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdResetMode|0x00|UINT8|0x0003F00D

