  ### @brief
  ### @details This control selects the SATA port hot plug capability. Note: 'ESP'
  ###  is External SATA Port, also known as E-SATA in the SATA spec. 5.2.6 e-SATA.
  ###  The hot-plug feature is described in SATA spec 5.2 Usage Models -
  ###  hot plug support. The control is a 64-bit value divided into bit fields.
  ###  Each bit represents one SATA port as follows:
  ### @li Bit 0-7: Socket0, SATA0 controller, Ports 0-7
  ### @li Bit 8-15: Socket0, SATA1 controller, Ports 0-7
  ### @li Bit 16-23: Socket0, SATA2 controller, Ports 0-7
  ### @li Bit 24-31: Socket0, SATA3 controller, Ports 0-7
  ### @li Bit 32-39: Socket1, SATA0 controller, Ports 0-7
  ### @li Bit 40-47: Socket1, SATA1 controller, Ports 0-7
  ### @li Bit 48-55: Socket1, SATA2 controller, Ports 0-7
  ### @li Bit 56-63: Socket1, SATA3 controller, Ports 0-7
  ### <p>For each bit field,
  ### @li  0b - hot plug feature is disabled.
  ### @li  1b - hot plug feature is enabled for the port.
  gEfiAmdAgesaModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdSataMultiDiePortESP|0x00|UINT64|0x0003F1E2

  gEfiAmdAgesaModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdSataMultiDieDevSlp|0x00|UINT64|0x0003F1E3             #bit8: Die1 DevSlp Port0 enable, bit9-11: port mapping
                                                                                               #bit12: Die1 DevSlp Port1 enable, bit13-15: port mapping
                                                                                               #bit16-23 Die2, etc.
  ### @brief Sata Activity LEDs
  ### @details This control specifies if each of the SATA controllers will use
  ### an SGPIO pin to show status/activity (e.g. via an LED). The value is split
  ###  into bit fields as follows:
  ### @li  bits 0-3: Socket 0 , SATA controllers 0-3.
  ### @li  bits 4-7: Socket 1 , SATA controllers 0-3.
  ### <p>For each bit field,
  ### @li  0b - No pin is used by this controller.
  ### @li  1b - SATA controller uses a SGPIO pin.
  gEfiAmdAgesaModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdSataSgpioMultiDieEnable|0x00|UINT8|0x0003F1E4

  gEfiAmdAgesaModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdALinkClkGateOff|0x01|UINT8|0x0003F201
  gEfiAmdAgesaModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdBLinkClkGateOff|0x01|UINT8|0x0003F202
  gEfiAmdAgesaModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdAbClockGating|0x01|UINT8|0x0003F203
  gEfiAmdAgesaModulePkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdSlowSpeedAbLinkClock|0x00|UINT8|0x0003F204
